  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 14-layer planar multilayer stack on aluminum substrate with air incidence. Stack sequence from incident side: SiO2 (Lemarchand) layer 1, Cr (Rakic-LD) layer 2, HfO2 layer 3, SiO2 (Lemarchand) layer 4, HfO2 layer 5, SiO2 (Lemarchand) layer 6, HfO2 layer 7, SiO2 (Lemarchand) layer 8, HfO2 layer 9, SiO2 (Lemarchand) layer 10, HfO2 layer 11, SiO2 (Lemarchand) layer 12, HfO2 layer 13, HfO2 layer 14, then Al (Rakic-LD) substrate. All 14 layer thicknesses are optimizable variables. Wavelength bands: 400-700 nm (target high absorptance, low reflectance), 700-2000 nm (target high reflectance). Incidence: normal, unpolarized. Materials: SiO2 (Lemarchand), hfo2, Cr (Rakic-LD), Al (Rakic-LD) as named in material catalog. Total layer count fixed at 14. Objective: maximize absorptance in 400-700 nm band while maximizing reflectance in 700-2000 nm band.",
